  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/baby-products/nursing-and-feeding/i-regret-buying-that-expensive-travel-high-chair-heres-what-i-should-have-bought-instead",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 36,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "I Regret Buying That $90 Travel High Chair. Here's What I Should Have Bought Instead",
        "text_sha256": "17491546b2a050c3d739887a14950a4867e75002f6a5c7dc5a07a969fae0869c",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Hiccapop Omniboost Travel High Chair",
        "text_sha256": "ceb3ac8484a0fb53083b3879698caa77923a93eb00ecd0602500c84931bef7ee",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Everyone swore I’d use this clip-on chair everywhere, but it just gathered dust in the basement.",
        "text_sha256": "10b6439b33ba395596e7f645be89835b63b613baaee7940a6c82cacc608c74f1",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Just so you know, What to Expect may earn commissions from the shopping links included on this page. All sales and prices are accurate at the time of publishing.",
        "text_sha256": "1922c3fea76d4f2a6f4ade63feb42972a2bb42e22c26d8117381d8356cd35012",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "I was shocked to discover how few restaurants actually have high chairs. Not just upscale spots, but “family-friendly” places with kids’ menus and crayons. Eating out with our six-month-old quickly became stressful. She’d scream in the stroller or thrash in our laps, so dining out started to feel like more trouble than it was worth.",
        "text_sha256": "4d30d2b1885378dd20171a91b49bff2f5accd997fd4b7bbc1c130c04418ef001",
        "word_count": 55
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The obvious solution was a travel high chair. And according to friends, coworkers, and basically every mom I knew, there was only one to get: the Inglesina Fast Table Chair. The $90 clip-on seat was supposed to be easy to set up, easy to carry, and something we’d use everywhere.",
        "text_sha256": "80a21a2fe9cbabcdea0348e072621236b197ca08062e314a059787c679949a9c",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "We didn’t.",
        "text_sha256": "fde07cefcc24e9b609c06eb13fa55f52a9d22fe675a842e53f1457c9ad583669",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The biggest issue was how often we couldn’t use it. Glass tables, thick lips, pedestal bases, tablecloths, suddenly half the places we went were off-limits. And when it did work, I never fully trusted it, which is not a great feeling mid-meal. The clamps either felt too tight on the table or not secure enough for a wiggly baby. My daughter also hated it, which didn’t help. With no footrest to stabilize her, she was constantly squirming and uncomfortable. And despite being marketed as “travel-friendly,” it was still bulky. Fine for the trunk, not ideal for a carry-on.",
        "text_sha256": "ac2e715d07d2d2f1299de23a8dce5f60cc8f80c8c18bcac5fb9216fd283b8e65",
        "word_count": 98
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Inglesina Fast Table Chair vs. Hiccapop Omni Booster Seat",
        "text_sha256": "2e39db94cb105f6d7b1eba57b5eec59342f5e45bbefe7702b830e3eaa50b50c3",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Even folded, the Inglesina Fast Table Chair is quite bulky. Especially compared to the Hiccapop Omni Booster Seat.",
        "text_sha256": "bf4cb2273b92d257b60e2978d983947756bc6af192a5cbf851c0e4992f7e73b1",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It took a family trip for me to realize what I actually needed. A friend pulled out the Hiccapop OmniBoost , basically a mini camping chair for babies, in the best way, popped it open, and strapped it onto a dining chair in under a minute. It was secure, stable, and didn’t depend on the table at all. It straps directly onto a standard chair and has a wide, sturdy base that keeps it in place, even with a wiggly toddler.",
        "text_sha256": "1a5cd5c7e23b6bb10fac14c729d54dc439d98cf0c029752b3673a0ceb3b30267",
        "word_count": 81
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Hiccapop Omni Booster Seat placed on a dining room chair",
        "text_sha256": "eccb2d4ce89c603f619467a25737661af8734e07e383a73393102dd2208b0d76",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "That night, the difference was obvious. My daughter sat awkwardly in a rental high chair, while my friend’s daughter was pulled right up to the table. Feeding her was easier, cleanup was easier, and there was no oversized tray to deal with. I ordered one before we even went to bed.",
        "text_sha256": "94eb2c98247520c08b9b0007f3ffde9b9969b293c2c5bf9d816be945b71eba4d",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Hiccapop Omni Booster Seat in the park with tray attachment",
        "text_sha256": "1643f8d44dbb4c256e35c55d27c541e9b57de2eba4675a8af2f0e5cc2bf129b7",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Four years later, we still use it all the time. It comes to the beach, the park, restaurants, or anywhere we need a reliable place to sit. It folds into a compact bag and fits easily in a stroller basket. The tray is removable and dishwasher-safe, which makes cleanup much easier than dealing with a full high chair setup. We even bought a second one for Grandma’s house, and together they still cost less than the one Inglesina chair now sitting unused in my basement.",
        "text_sha256": "e01df45d6f16a36538e3bd67fc02d841538a7caa34f229e6facad77ba4da647d",
        "word_count": 85
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your baby needs a place to sit, but it doesn’t need to be complicated. If I could go back, I’d skip the clip-on chair, grab the Hiccapop OmniBoost , and put that extra $50 toward a much-needed glass of wine at our next family dinner.",
        "text_sha256": "b2096306edecb30cdd40061e995c01b4615df613258abc26af95670facc59034",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h4",
        "text": "Hiccapop OmniBoost Travel High Chair",
        "text_sha256": "fc841ef96a2182ceff185c0dbcbd9002e35b4fb9360339666060a042787774fd",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "The Chair You'll Use Everywhere",
        "text_sha256": "2729f086d5b101781a04ea8ca5ddac7d755e5eee4a202d3324dc0632585a9423",
